Z||000000||Will||03-28-2001||10:18 PM||||This was posted on my local car club list:<P> <A HREF="http://www.bmwclub.org.hk/gallery/crash.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.bmwclub.org.hk/gallery/crash.html</A> <P>This happened at Willow Springs last year during the Ferrari of Beverly<BR>Hills event introducing the 360 Modena. Ferrari owners were invited to<BR>run their own cars on the track, while seeing the new 360, as well as an<BR>ex-Eddie Irvine F1 car and a 333 SP. The owner of this F50 went wide on<BR>the outside of the exit at turn one, shot across the track and kept<BR>going until finally hitting the 4-5 foot high dirt berm at the end of<BR>the track area. From there it smashed into bits, flew over the berm and<BR>finally stopped when it hit the chain-link fence around the kart track<P>It's probably hard to look cool in front of the rest of your Ferrari<BR>buddies when you just totalled your F50. I bet you also stop getting<BR>Christmas cards from your insurance agent.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Will (edited 03-28-2001).]||||reg||1
